  "_comment": "M185 (docs/LINK_PREVIEWS.md §2, §4.1): the link cards under a message, the same on the three clients. keys: a link's key for MessageOut.hidden_previews (scheme and host in lower case, fragment dropped, '/' for an empty path, the rest as written; null for anything but http(s)); the server's link_cards.preview_key gives the same. cards: which cards a message shows (the clients' rule, base_url being the server the app is logged into): `messages` are the message links' cards (each linked message once, at most 3, not the message itself, the URL of its first link), `external` the link that gets the Open Graph card (the first link that is not a message or drive link of this server; none when the message announces a call); links in code count for nothing; a card whose link's key is in `hidden` is left out and nothing takes its place. A body's links (2026-11-05) are the links its tokenizer reads (apps/shared/inline-format.json: a `[label](url)` link's URL, a bare URL without the closing mark or the Japanese after it, links in code and emphasis are none). body_keys: the keys of a body's links, in order, each once (the clients compute exactly these; the server's link_cards.link_keys holds them and more). legacy_keys: keys stored before 2026-11-05 under the old reading (a URL up to a space, `<`, `>`, `)` or `]`, trailing .,!?;:。、」』） dropped) and what migration 0132 makes of them (the key of the same link read now; a right or unknown key stays). Server: tests/test_message_link_cards.py (keys, body_keys, legacy_keys); Desktop / Web: tests/messageLinkCards.test.tsx; iOS and Android read keys, cards and body_keys.",
